Did some testing on this subject:

Tame leprechauns do drop gold, but they also teleport away as soon as 
they steal it then drop it immediately. Which sometimes means searching 
the whole level for where they dropped it, if you don't notice them 
immediately.

It's pretty tough to avoid the priest, temples aren't that big. Also, 
leprechauns do normal damage and will attack you aplenty even without 
gold visible, so this is a dangerous stunt.

A tame leprechaun apparently steals ALL the gold of the target (test 
quantity: 110,000). So it only takes one lucky hit. I've found it 
easiest actually to only have one pet leper and hope it hits the priest 
before the priest hits it. When I had an entire room full of them and 
the priest, they slaughtered each other before any of them even tried 
hitting the priest.

So if you want to try this trick, be sure you're durable and then 
reverse geno them in a seperate room. Tame one at a time and bring them 
to the priest, put on conflict, when it hits the priest, remove conflict 
ASAP then put on the towel. Run over to where the leprechaun teleported 
to to collect the gold (and hope it wasn't a shop).

